Venoco - Exiting position still under negotiation with Venoco. EA recently gained seat on Board of Directors. 
Advanced Mobile Power Systems (AMPS) - EA is closing company and severing employees. Appraiser sought to 
determine market value of units. 
Utiliquest - EA is selling its interest to GFI Energy Ventures with closing anticipated in Q3 2001. Gain is expected. 
Troubled (Equity) / Non-Performing (Debt) 
Catalytica - Filing S-1 for secondary offering which should close by mid August. 
Industrial Holdings - Merger with T-3 Energy Q3 2001 with terms providing for payment in full upon closing. Closing 
on schedule. 
Oconto Falls Debt (transferred from ENA Clo #1) - Missed 6/20/01 quarterly interest payment of $353M. Enron drew on 
letter of credit supporting debt interest for payment. EA assumed management of Company in Q3 2001. 
Octagon -The Company is in breach of loan covenants and needs cash within one month or face insolvency. 
Heartland Steel - Sold in Chapter 11 auction, 6/2001, for $50MM. EA's holding of Heartland's sub-debt and equity worthless. 
Hughes Rawls - Final dissolution of partnership is pending final approval of withdrawal applications from various states. 
Mshow.com - Accutel is assuming operating responsibility for the Company. 
Crown Energy - Arbitration proceedings related to MCNIC's demand for payment of $15MM debt began on 7/23/01. 
WB Oil Company - Dissolution of partnership is complete. No further obligation to EA. 
